---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About | Data With Duke">
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-20">
    <header class="mb-16 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-5xl font-black text-blue-900 mb-6">The Dreaded Ts & Cs with a dash of Ws</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        What we need from you if you want to use this site...
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-slate lg:prose-xl max-w-none 
                prose-headings:text-blue-900 prose-headings:font-bold
                prose-p:leading-relaxed">
      
      <h2>...Actually, it's not much!</h2>
      <p>
        This project is a grower - in reality it started as a hobby and a way to learn and practice new skills
        while sharing some skills we'd already picked up along the way. This means that although functionality of this site is 
        quite limited right now, there is ambition to grow it into something magical. Like an enchanted forest of 1s and 0s.
        But for now, the only Terms we're thrusting onto you are the boring legalities of product ownership.
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        "Intellectual Property and Copyright"
      </blockquote>

      <h2>What we own</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The Content:</strong> All blogs, podcasts, lessons, images and other content visible on this site</li>
        <li><strong>The Data:</strong> Any data we share remains our property. If you want to use it for any other purpose than highlighted on the site, let us know</li>
        <li><strong>That's it:</strong> Enjoy!</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="mt-12 p-8 bg-blue-50 rounded-3xl border border-blue-100">
        <h3 class="mt-0">What about Privacy?</h3>
        <p class="mb-0">
          Right now, our data gathering processes are very light...  
          check out our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy here</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>